WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
Hello BFFs!

2
00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.070
Hi, to everyone here in this room,

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.220
that I am so lucky to get to be with all the time.

4
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.947
It is Monday!
(audience cheering)

5
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:15.780
I have to admit,

6
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.320
I woke up really nervous about what to say, whew today.

7
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.620
'Cause it's a big day.

8
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.100
And when we were doing this pilot for this show,

9
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.180
it was like an audition tape in 2019,

10
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.370
my bosses and I spoke.

11
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:33.600
And we were concerned about how not to be political.

12
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.740
And we knew that we were going to be launching

13
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.010
in an election year, et cetera.

14
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.847
And my immediate thought was,

15
00:00:40.847 --> 00:00:42.847
"God, I hate, authority!

16
00:00:42.847 --> 00:00:46.340
I don't want to have to censor myself!"

17
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.723
But then I realized, calmly,

18
00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:52.610
that they were trying not to be polarizing.

19
00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.530
And I understood that because at my very core beliefs,

20
00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.370
I am anything but political.

21
00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.720
One thing I wanted to do

22
00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.160
on the show was avoid our differences

23
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.620
and find something that we all have in common.

24
00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.100
And then 2020 happened.

25
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.380
And the whole world changed.

26
00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:16.140
And we did have something that united all of us.

27
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.760
A pandemic which wasn't political

28
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.290
until it was absolutely political.

29
00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.530
And then black lives matter ignited

30
00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.960
in the most important way, and I jumped in.

31
00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.640
And I knew that I would possibly have a talk show coming.

32
00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.330
And at some point I would have to start talking

33
00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:38.100
and find my voice.

34
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:41.340
And I've been finding my voice on Instagram for years.

35
00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:45.120
But usually about pretty tamed things.

36
00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.310
Beauty, love, and fun, positivity, and joy.

37
00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:51.090
And it's a good thing I've been practicing talking

38
00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.440
to a camera for years by myself.

39
00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.166
Because well, welcome to this show.

40
00:01:57.166 --> 00:01:58.390
(audience laughing)

41
00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:00.100
As Saturday night live says

42
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.000
I'm a girl alone in a big studio, having fun.

43
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.587
Someone's having fun in 2020.

44
00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:07.020
That's my favorite line

45
00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.820
from the whole show, the whole thing.

46
00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:14.440
And I have had moments where I then didn't even want to get

47
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.820
on social media this year.

48
00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.320
As if a post didn't match the magnitude of the moment.

49
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.260
But let's face it,

50
00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.750
social media is now the most powerful thing we've had.

51
00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.850
And I've been finding my way on social for years.

52
00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.890
And now I get to do this show.

53
00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.430
And so I thought very quietly about what I could say today

54
00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.780
about this moment in our country.

55
00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:40.150
And I think it is wonderful that I got to sit

56
00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.563
with my daughters and see them imagine their own potential.

57
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:50.440
Because every human is full of equal possibilities.

58
00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.260
And I didn't want to post, and I didn't want to gloat

59
00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:57.070
because I know there are people out there who are hurting.

60
00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.190
There are people who are not happy about this.

61
00:02:59.190 --> 00:03:02.877
And I am naive, but I always think, and I understand

62
00:03:02.877 --> 00:03:06.180
that I want to continue this show

63
00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:07.610
to be a safe space for everyone,

64
00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.410
no matter what your priorities are.

65
00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:13.120
And what I am overwhelmed

66
00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:16.240
with is not a win for this country.

67
00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.090
But the divine intervention of 2020 itself.

68
00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.570
The worldwide reset.

69
00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:24.930
The year that challenged the entire globe

70
00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.820
and continues to do so.

71
00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:30.280
And that this moment is about hearing those cries

72
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.581
for help and to get to a place of decency and respect.

73
00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:38.940
Respect for the world we live in and everyone in it.

74
00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.400
So this is the year we should

75
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.750
remember when we asked what works?

76
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.160
And challenged ourselves about every answer.

77
00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.030
Do schools work?

78
00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.540
Does the economy work?

79
00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.990
Does it serve everyone?

80
00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:52.270
How do we tackle healthcare?

81
00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.810
How do we be a better neighbor?

82
00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.890
The year that forced us to imagine,

83
00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.859
re-imagine everything.

84
00:03:59.859 --> 00:04:01.970
This year, when my daughter, Frankie,

85
00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.330
asked me what the meaning of life was,

86
00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:05.950
I was like, " Cool."

87
00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.930
I had a moment of divine intervention.

88
00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.670
I did, I closed my eyes

89
00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:13.120
and the answer was so loud and unobstructed.

90
00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.467
And I opened my eyes and I said to her,

91
00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.140
"Frankie, I believe the meaning

92
00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.810
of life is we are here to take care of each other."

93
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.560
So yes, I don't want to be political.

94
00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:28.240
I want to be out of the fight and into the human solution.

95
00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.490
How do we take care of each other, and be respectful,

96
00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:34.060
and good, aware, and kind?

97
00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:37.810
Calm the waters, act local, get global,

98
00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.500
look around with a new level of imagination.

99
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.520
We have life and love, children and humanity in common.

100
00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.800
Let's take off our armor!

101
00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.823
And get into position to be problem solvers together.

102
00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:55.225
And this is gonna be the oddest segue ever (laughs).

103
00:04:55.225 --> 00:04:58.392
(audience applauding)

104
00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.340
But I've been wanting to do a thing

105
00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.100
on this show called word of the week.

106
00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.550
Now again, cause we discuss every little thing,

107
00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.023
every little detail of the show.

108
00:05:11.023 --> 00:05:14.000
We were worried, does it feel like a lesson?

109
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.430
And then I had to say, "Heck yeah,

110
00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:16.263
because we're all students."

111
00:05:16.263 --> 00:05:19.791
And I've been holding onto this word for weeks waiting,

112
00:05:19.791 --> 00:05:22.740
sitting on it like a nest egg.

113
00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.510
And it's perfect for today.

114
00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.850
So,
(book crashing)

115
00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.300
this is my dictionary.

116
00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.950
It's important to me.

117
00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.760
All right, let's roll the graphic.

118
00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.190
Word of the week?

119
00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:34.880
Yes!

120
00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:38.410
And our inaugural word is: My dictionary is upside down.

121
00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:42.183
That should tell you everything, is intrepid.

122
00:05:42.183 --> 00:05:44.440
(audience applauding)
Yes!

123
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.360
Characterized by resolute fearlessness,

124
00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.340
fortitude, and endurance.

125
00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.150
So let's be intrepid, 2020!

126
00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:54.990
And let's use that word of the week all week

127
00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.750
and squeeze it in when it fits or even it doesn't.

128
00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.080
And by Friday, hopefully, being fearless

129
00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.400
will invade our bodies and our minds,

130
00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.600
as we head into the end of the year.

131
00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:10.600
And into a brand new one with hope and respect,

132
00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:15.724
and a time where we take care of each other.

133
00:06:15.724 --> 00:06:18.307 line:15%
(upbeat music)

